! mcp_bootstrap_p90.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 90:
! the tail of the unit-area-table generator inside the MOVE
! sub-routine -- "GENERATE THE UNIT AREA TABLES" and "MODIFY THE
! CHAN/UNIT STATUS TABLES".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.97, header "PAGE NUMBER 90",
! card ids 18000383..18000438, LOCATION 005115 in the header.
!
! Fifty-six listing lines, thirty-nine of which compile.
! First printed location 005115.00, last 005154.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE DOES <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-8 finish the loop that builds one entry of the unit
! table: fetch the reference number, store the 64-bit unit name,
! store the new entry, step the table counter in T UNXW+28, and
! save the pointer in T DKSAV.  Lines 16-36 are "GENERATE THE UNIT
! AREA TABLES": the channel address and number go in, and if the
! channel is multi-unit the unit number goes in too; if the type is
! tape the system-tape bit is set, a reel-pool slot is taken, its
! first reel zeroed and labelled, the pool index stepped and
! bounds-checked, and an over-run goes to T MREJB with code 4 in
! T MX1.  Lines 42-56 are "MODIFY THE CHAN/UNIT STATUS TABLES":
! compute the unit-table address, set the SEL bit, store the unit
! area table address, carry the ownership bit over from .26($15),
! set the assigned bit, reset the not-overlap-reserved bit, and
! leave two indexes straddling the table.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE STAND-INS BELOW ARE READ OFF THIS PAGE'S OWN BINARY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! No symbol this page uses is defined on this page, and pp.86-89
! have no decks yet, so the deck cannot assemble without stand-ins.
! Rather than guess them, every one is taken from the BINARY OUTPUT
! column of the very row that uses it, which is printed primary
! source.  The decoding used, established against decks/
! mcp_bootstrap_p80.strap where both sides are known:
!
!   a half-word prints as  AAAAAA.BB CC  = address(18 bits, octal)
!   . six more bits (octal) . opcode byte (hex).
!
!   INDEX OPS (one half-word): BB = [half-word bit][index(4)][1].
!     p80 line 9 "SV,TIXG,TNEXT", T NEXT = (8)3264.40, prints
!     003264.61 30 -- 0o61 = 1 1000 1, half-word bit 1 for the .40
!     and 1000 = 8 for T IXG = $8.
!
!   VFL OPS (two half-words): the first half-word is the operand's
!   bit address and the opcode byte's low nibble is the index; the
!   second half-word carries the field length in bits 3-8 and half
!   the third operand in bits 10-17.
!     p80 line 17 "L,TUNCT(TIXG),46", T UNCT = SYN(BU,8),0.28,
!     prints 000000.34 88  010027.20 50 -- 0o34 = 28, nibble 8 =
!     T IXG, length bits = 001000 = 8, and 0o027 low bits = 23 = 46/2.
!
! LINE 4's THIRD OPERAND IS "04" AND THE ASSEMBLER AGREES: the
! third operand is encoded in the second half-word, line 4's
! !CHECK on 014002.06 70 passes with the deck reading ",04", and
! ",64" or ",46" would have produced a different word.  The same
! field also halves the operand into bits 10-17 -- 4 -> 2 on line
! 4, 64 -> 32 on line 5, 46 -> 23 on line 17 -- which is how the
! glyph was read in the first place.
!
! A stand-in's NAME is read from the STATEMENT column; its VALUE
! and LENGTH are read from the BINARY OUTPUT column of the same
! row, which is cited after each.  Nothing here is inferred from
! what the name sounds like.  THREE ARE EXCEPTIONS AND ARE MARKED:
! T MULTI (line 21), T TYPE (line 24) and T UNRES (line 52) are the
! operands of a BZB or a BBZ, and a branch-on-bit prints its target
! in the second half-word instead of a length, so for those three
! only the bit address is read and the (BU,1) is the op's own
! one-bit operand, not something the column printed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> WHAT THIS DECK'S CHECKS DO AND DO NOT PROVE <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Most stand-ins are read out of the same field the !CHECK then
! compares against, so those rows re-report their own input.  What
! is NOT circular, and passes:
!
!   * the OPCODE BYTE of all thirty-nine rows.  It comes from the
!     mnemonic and the index register, never from a stand-in's
!     value, so it is an independent test of the statement column:
!     8A 8F 83 86 87 88 80 48 C2 42 90 30 38 36 10 05 07 06 00
!     50 D0 F0 70 B0 01.
!   * all five SYMBOLS.  They depend only on half-word counts --
!     two for a VFL op, one for an index op -- which no stand-in
!     can move.
!   * the FOURTEEN ROWS WITH NO STAND-IN IN THEM end to end: lines
!     6, 18, 30, 32, 35, 43, 46, 48, 55, 56 carry only literals,
!     and lines 21, 24, 34, 52 branch to labels on this page, so
!     their 005146.34, 005143.74, 005143.72 and 005153.74 are
!     computed from this deck's own layout and check T M1DA,
!     T M1DAA and T M1DX a second time, against the instruction
!     stream rather than the location column.
!
! Circular by construction: the first half-word's address and the
! second half-word's length on the twenty-two rows whose operand is
! a derived symbol.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> CONTINUITY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 7's T UNXW is 004653.00, which is exactly where printed
! p.84 line 4 puts "T UNXW  XW,TUNATB,0,$0".  The page's own
! location column also closes on itself: every one of the thirty-
! nine deltas is 0.40 for a one-half-word row and 1.00 for a
! two-half-word row, carries included (005117 -> 005120,
! 005137.40 -> 005140.00, 005147.40 -> 005150.40).
!
! A SECOND, MACHINE READING OF THE LOCATION COLUMN.
! "python3 strap/mcp_ocr.py 90" recovers twenty of the thirty-nine
! locations, and all twenty agree with the eye (its "065123.00" for
! 005123.00 is a dropped-digit OCR slip of the kind that file warns
! about, not a disagreement about the page).  It flagged nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 35's OPCODE BYTE READS C1 AND IS 01 <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The only row where the first assemble disagreed with the eye, so
! it was re-rendered at 1800 dpi BEFORE the assembler's answer was
! taken, the way decks/mcp_bootstrap_p80.strap describes.
!
! THE ROW'S OWN ZEROS DECIDE IT.  Line 35 prints
!
!     000004.03 01     as   C C C C C 4 . C 3   C 1
!
! -- a weak-impression row in which EVERY zero comes out open on
! the right, including the four in "000004" and the one in ".03",
! which cannot be anything but zeros.  The byte's first glyph has
! exactly that shape.  Line 1, three inches up the same column,
! prints "005162.36 C2": there the zeros are CLOSED ovals and the
! byte's first glyph is open, a shape unlike that row's zeros --
! and C2 is what the assembler independently produces for BAE.
! So the page prints a real C and a worn 0 in the same column, and
! what separates them is the other zeros in the same row, not the
! opening itself.
!
! The structure agrees: enc_imm_index lays out
! imm(19) J(4) 10000(5) code(4), so an immediate-index op's byte is
! 0000cccc and its high nibble CANNOT be C.  Lines 32 and 56 --
! V+I, byte 05 -- and printed p.80's V+ICR, byte 07, print the same
! way and match.  p.80 records C5 -> 05 and C7 -> 07 as two of the
! seven earlier cases of this exact glyph on this exact format.

        SLC, (8)5115.0

! ---- index names, read from the index field of the rows that use
!      them (and from the operand addresses of lines 26 and 55,
!      where an index register appears as its memory word, 16+n) --
TMX1    SYN, $1              ! line 35  BB = 0o03 -> index 1
TMXB    SYN, $3              ! lines 17,22,24  opcode 83 -> 3
TMXD    SYN, $5              ! line 16  BB = 0o13 -> index 5
TMXE    SYN, $6              ! line 56  BB = 0o15 -> 6; line 55
                             !          addresses it as word 0o26
TMXF    SYN, $7              ! line 32  BB = 0o17 -> 7; line 26
                             !          addresses it as word 0o27
TMXG    SYN, $8              ! lines 8,18  BB = 0o21/0o20 -> 8
TMXEE   SYN, $9              ! line 55  BB = 0o22 -> index 9
TMXI    SYN, $10             ! line 4   opcode 8A -> 10

! ---- words, read from the address field of the rows that use them
TCHSXW  SYN, (8)2152.0       ! line 19  002152.00
TBAMCP  SYN, (8)2153.0       ! line 33  002153.16, BB bit 0 = 0
TDKSAV  SYN, (8)4652.0       ! line 8   004652.21, BB bit 0 = 0
TUNXW   SYN, (8)4653.0       ! line 7   004653.34 (= printed p.84)
TM1A    SYN, (8)5107.40      ! line 2   005107.61, BB bit 0 = 1
TM1D    SYN, (8)5162.0       ! line 1   005162.36
TMREJB  SYN, (8)5377.0       ! line 36  005377.10

! ---- table offsets, read from the first half-word's bit address
!      and the second half-word's length field -------------------
TIREF   SYN(BU,12), 0.52     ! line 4   000000.64 / len 001100
TUNME   SYN(BU,48), 25.0     ! line 5   000031.00.  The len 000000
                             !          in this row is the STATEMENT's
                             !          own (BU,64), not the symbol's;
                             !          printed p.84 line 9 defines
                             !          TUNME as (BU,48).
TFIAAC  SYN(BU,18), 3.0             ! line 16  000003.13 (an index op)
TABSCH  SYN(BU,18), 0.46     ! line 17  000000.56 / len 010010
TCHANN  SYN(BU,7), 0.12      ! line 20  000000.14 / len 000111
TMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27      ! line 21  000000.33 (BZB, one bit)
TABSUN  SYN(BU,3), 0.7       ! line 22  000000.07 / len 000011
TUNITN  SYN(BU,3), 0.47      ! line 23  000000.57 / len 000011
TTYPE   SYN(BU,4), 0.3       ! line 24  000000.03 -- BZB PRINTS NO
                             !          LENGTH, so this page cannot
                             !          see it; (BU,4) is printed p.62
                             !          line 33, which defines it.
TSYSTM  SYN(BU,1), 7.25      ! line 25  000007.31 / len 000001
TFRLAD  SYN(BU,18), 8.0      ! line 27  000010.00 / len 010010
TCREEL  SYN(BU,18), 8.32     ! line 28  000010.40 / len 010010
TREELK  SYN(BU,7), 8.57      ! line 29  000010.71 / len 000111
TRELB   SYN(BU,1), 0.27      ! line 31  000000.33, (BU,1) printed
TUNTBA  SYN(BU,18), 0.0      ! line 42  000000.00 / len 010010
TSEL    SYN(BU,1), 0.39      ! line 44  000000.47 / len 000001
TCHOWN  SYN(BU,1), 0.32      ! line 49  000000.40 / len 000001
TUNASG  SYN(BU,1), 0.29      ! line 51  000000.35 / len 000001
TUNRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.62      ! line 52  000000.76 (BBZ, one bit)
TOVRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.63      ! line 53  000000.77 / len 000001

        SLC, (8)5115.0

! ---- the page, as printed -----------------------------------------
        BAE,TM1D                     ! line 1  -UNIT AREA TABLE GENERATED
TM1B    CB+,TMXG,TM1A                ! line 2
TM1E    LF,TIREF(TMXI),04            ! line 4  -GET THE REF. NUMBER
        SF(BU,64),TUNME(TMXG),64     ! line 5
        CM0101(BU,64),0.0(TMXG)      ! line 6  -STORE NEW ENTRY IN TABLE
        M+1(BU,18),TUNXW+28          ! line 7  -STEP TABLE COUNTER
        SV,TMXG,TDKSAV               ! line 8

! ---- GENERATE THE UNIT AREA TABLES (lines 12-14) ------------------
        SV,TMXD,TFIAAC(TMXE)         ! line 16 -FILE AREA ACT. ADDRESS
        L,TABSCH(TMXB),46            ! line 17 -GET THE ADDR OF THE
                                      !          ASSIGNED CHAN
        LX,TMXG,$R                   ! line 18 -CHAN TABLE ADDR TO IX
        -(BU,18),TCHSXW,46           ! line 19 -COMPUTE THE CHANNEL NUMBER
        ST,TCHANN(TMXE),46           ! line 20
        BZB,TMULTI(TMXG),TM1DA       ! line 21 -IF NOT A MULTI UNIT CHAN
        L,TABSUN(TMXB),46            ! line 22 -GET THE UNIT NUMBER
        ST,TUNITN(TMXE),46           ! line 23 -AND PLACE IN UNIT AREA TBL
        BZB,TTYPE(TMXB),TM1DAA       ! line 24 -IF THE TYPE IS NOT TAPE
        CM1111,TSYSTM(TMXE)          ! line 25 -SET THE SYSTEM TAPE BIT
                                      !          FOR INITIAL
        C0011(BU,18),TMXF            ! line 26 -GET REEL POOL ADDRESS
        CM0101,TFRLAD(TMXE)          ! line 27 -AND STORE IN UNIT AREA
        CM0101,TCREEL(TMXE)          ! line 28
        M+1,TREELK(TMXE)             ! line 29 -SET THE REEL COUNT TO ONE
        Z,0.0(TMXF)                  ! line 30 -ZERO THE FIRST REEL SLOT
        CM1111(BU,1),TRELB(TMXF)     ! line 31
        V+I,TMXF,1.0                 ! line 32 -STEP REEL POOL INDEX
        KV,TMXF,TBAMCP               ! line 33 -IS THE REEL POOL
                                      !          EXCEEDING BOUNDS
        BXL,TM1DAA                   ! line 34 -NO
        LVI,TMX1,4.0                 ! line 35 -YES SO NOTE IT JC
        B,TMREJB                     ! line 36 -AND REJECT JOB

! ---- MODIFY THE CHAN/UNIT STATUS TABLES (lines 38-40) -------------
TM1DAA  +,TUNTBA(TMXG),46            ! line 42 -COMPUTE UNIT TABLE ADDR.
                                      !          IN MULTI CASE
        LV,TMXG,$R                   ! line 43 -GET POINTER FOR UNIT TABLE
        CM1111,TSEL(TMXG)            ! line 44 -SET THE SEL BIT TO 1 FOR
                                      !          ALL MULTI CH
TM1DA   SV,TMXE,0.0(TMXG)            ! line 46 -STORE UNIT AREA TBL ADDRESS
        LF(BU,1),.26($15)            ! line 48 -GET THE OWNERSHIP BIT
        SF,TCHOWN(TMXG)              ! line 49
        CM0000,TUNASG(TMXG)          ! line 51 -SET THE UNIT ASSIGNED BIT
        BBZ,TUNRES(TMXG),TM1DX       ! line 52 -RESET THE NOT OV RES FIRST
        CM0000,TOVRES(TMXG)          ! line 53 -
TM1DX   LV,TMXEE,TMXE                ! line 55 -KEEP ONE IX TO BEGINNING
                                      !          OF TBL
        V+I,TMXE,9.0                 ! line 56 -ADVANCE THE OTHER TO END + 1

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 90 -----------------
!SYM   TM1B     005115.40
!SYM   TM1E     005116.00
!SYM   TM1DAA   005143.40
!SYM   TM1DA    005146.00
!SYM   TM1DX    005153.40
!CHECK 005115.00 | 005162.36 C2 | line 1  BAE,TM1D
!CHECK 005115.40 | 005107.61 48 | line 2  T M1B  CB+,TMXG,TM1A
!CHECK 005116.00 | 000000.64 8A  014002.06 70 | line 4  T M1E  LF,TIREF(TMXI),04
!CHECK 005117.00 | 000031.00 88  000040.12 F0 | line 5  SF(BU,64),TUNME(TMXG),64
!CHECK 005120.00 | 000000.00 88  000000.12 F0 | line 6  CM0101(BU,64),0.0(TMXG)
!CHECK 005121.00 | 004653.34 80  022000.22 B0 | line 7  M+1(BU,18),TUNXW+28
!CHECK 005122.00 | 004652.21 30 | line 8  SV,TMXG,TDKSAV
!CHECK 005122.40 | 000003.13 36 | line 16  SV,TMXD,TFIAAC(TMXE)
!CHECK 005123.00 | 000000.56 83  022027.20 50 | line 17  L,TABSCH(TMXB),46
!CHECK 005124.00 | 000011.20 10 | line 18  LX,TMXG,$R
!CHECK 005124.40 | 002152.00 80  022027.30 10 | line 19  -(BU,18),TCHSXW,46
!CHECK 005125.40 | 000000.14 86  007027.20 D0 | line 20  ST,TCHANN(TMXE),46
!CHECK 005126.40 | 000000.33 88  005146.34 00 | line 21  BZB,TMULTI(TMXG),TM1DA
!CHECK 005127.40 | 000000.07 83  003027.20 50 | line 22  L,TABSUN(TMXB),46
!CHECK 005130.40 | 000000.57 86  003027.20 D0 | line 23  ST,TUNITN(TMXE),46
!CHECK 005131.40 | 000000.03 83  005143.74 00 | line 24  BZB,TTYPE(TMXB),TM1DAA
!CHECK 005132.40 | 000007.31 86  001000.36 F0 | line 25  CM1111,TSYSTM(TMXE)
!CHECK 005133.40 | 000027.00 80  022000.06 70 | line 26  C0011(BU,18),TMXF
!CHECK 005134.40 | 000010.00 86  022000.12 F0 | line 27  CM0101,TFRLAD(TMXE)
!CHECK 005135.40 | 000010.40 86  022000.12 F0 | line 28  CM0101,TCREEL(TMXE)
!CHECK 005136.40 | 000010.71 86  007000.22 B0 | line 29  M+1,TREELK(TMXE)
!CHECK 005137.40 | 000000.22 07 | line 30  Z,0.0(TMXF)
!CHECK 005140.00 | 000000.33 87  001000.36 F0 | line 31  CM1111(BU,1),TRELB(TMXF)
!CHECK 005141.00 | 000001.17 05 | line 32  V+I,TMXF,1.0
!CHECK 005141.40 | 002153.16 90 | line 33  KV,TMXF,TBAMCP
!CHECK 005142.00 | 005143.72 42 | line 34  BXL,TM1DAA
!CHECK 005142.40 | 000004.03 01 | line 35  LVI,TMX1,4.0  -- see the note on line 35's opcode byte
!CHECK 005143.00 | 005377.10 00 | line 36  B,TMREJB
!CHECK 005143.40 | 000000.00 88  022027.20 10 | line 42  T M1DAA  +,TUNTBA(TMXG),46
!CHECK 005144.40 | 000011.20 30 | line 43  LV,TMXG,$R
!CHECK 005145.00 | 000000.47 88  001000.36 F0 | line 44  CM1111,TSEL(TMXG)
!CHECK 005146.00 | 000000.15 38 | line 46  T M1DA  SV,TMXE,0.0(TMXG)
!CHECK 005146.40 | 000000.32 8F  001000.06 70 | line 48  LF(BU,1),.26($15)
!CHECK 005147.40 | 000000.40 88  001000.12 F0 | line 49  SF,TCHOWN(TMXG)
!CHECK 005150.40 | 000000.35 88  001000.00 F0 | line 51  CM0000,TUNASG(TMXG)
!CHECK 005151.40 | 000000.76 88  005153.74 06 | line 52  BBZ,TUNRES(TMXG),TM1DX
!CHECK 005152.40 | 000000.77 88  001000.00 F0 | line 53  CM0000,TOVRES(TMXG)
!CHECK 005153.40 | 000026.22 30 | line 55  T M1DX  LV,TMXEE,TMXE
!CHECK 005154.00 | 000011.15 05 | line 56  V+I,TMXE,9.0
